.TH WAYFIRE-MODS 1 "2026" "wayfire-mods" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
wayfire-mods \- build a Wayland compositor stack (wlroots + Wayfire + plugins)
from source
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B setup.sh
[\fBinstall\fR|\fBverify\fR|\fBcheck\fR|\fBuninstall\fR|\fBtest\fR|\
\fBversion\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B wayfire-mods
builds a complete from-source Wayland compositor stack into a self-contained
prefix: wlroots (clean upstream), Wayfire (with a small set of patches), wcm,
wayfire-plugins-extra and wf-info (clean upstream), the filters and pixdecor
decorators (with patches), and a set of custom Wayfire plugins. The upstream
components are fetched at pinned refs and assembled onto pristine checkouts, so
each patch and plugin stays a discrete unit and the base is refreshed by bumping
a ref rather than by maintaining a fork.
.PP
wlroots and Wayfire are ABI-coupled; both, and every satellite, are pinned
together in
.IR refs .
Every installed ELF carries a relative
.RB ( <prefix>/lib/<arch> )
rpath, so the prefix resolves with no ld.so.conf entry.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B install
Build and install the stack into the system prefix (default
.IR /opt/wayfire ,
root). Incremental: each component skips when its artifact and stamp are
current, so a converged prefix is a no-op. Sudo-safe: if the prefix is not
writable and no non-interactive sudo is available, it skips cleanly rather than
block on a prompt.
.TP
.B verify
Build into a throwaway prefix and discard it, with no sudo, proving the whole
stack still fetches, patches, and compiles against the pins without touching the
real prefix. Run this before bumping an upstream ref.
.TP
.B check
Report whether Wayfire is installed, self-contained by rpath, and its key
components present, as
.RB [ OK ]/[ FAIL ]
markers.
.TP
.B uninstall
Remove the prefix and the build stamps.
.TP
.B version
Print the package version and the wlroots/Wayfire pins.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I refs
The upstream URLs and pinned refs (wlroots, Wayfire, wcm, plugins-extra,
filters, wf-info, pixdecor).
.TP
.I patches/
Patches applied onto the Wayfire, filters, and pixdecor checkouts.
.TP
.I plugins/
The custom Wayfire plugins, built against the installed Wayfire.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/wayfire-mods/
The upstream checkouts, build trees, and per-component stamps.
.SH NOTES
The greeter/session stack (greetd, the login sway config, swaylock, ReGreet) is
NOT part of this package; it is wired by the consumer.
